{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And a cut.</b> Also the corner of the head and of the beard are known from words of tradition." "And the word <b>for the soul.</b> The dead body, and so it is translated, and this is the truth. And the nun was not given a dagesh to lighten the language." "<b>And a tattoo inscription.</b> Some say it is connected with 'and a cut for the soul,' for there is one who marks his body with a known form by fire for the dead, and even today there are those who mark in their youth on their faces to be distinguished. And the word <b>qa'qa.</b> is doubled like רוקע הארץ וצאצאיה (who spread out the earth and its offspring) and it is from the root of והוקע אותם (and he impaled them). And according to the translator it too is a foreign word; this too is correct."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:07.781703317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}